<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rijeka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fiume</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rijeka, Italian Fiume, is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kvarner-gulf">Kvarner Gulf</a> of the Adriatic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s main port under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, it was disputed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, occupied by D'Annunzio in 1919, made a free state in 1920 and annexed by Italy in 1924. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it passed to Yugoslavia and most Italians left.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rijeka.jpg" alt="Rijeka" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio199cro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rijeka_Riva_promenade_aerial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
